<section class="content-section" id="overview-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Gratuity Calculations and Compliance in Delhi</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - Gratuity Calculations & Compliance in Delhi Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p>The Payment of Gratuity Act, 1972 (now in Code on Social Security, 2020) mandates gratuity by every Delhi employer with 10+ employees. Formula: (Last Drawn Salary × 15 × Completed Years) / 26. Eligibility: 5 years continuous service (death/disablement: no minimum). Fixed-term employees qualify after 1 year pro-rata under new codes. Maximum Rs 20 lakh. Payment within 30 days; delay attracts 10% p.a. interest. Wages must be ≥50% of CTC under new codes, increasing gratuity base. Patron handles calculations, provisioning, and compliance from our Delhi office.</p>
                </div>
                <p>Delhi has one of India's highest concentrations of establishments with 10+ employees - IT companies in Nehru Place and CP, BPO operations, manufacturing in Okhla and Naraina, hospitality in Aerocity, retail chains, consulting firms, and startups that scaled beyond 10 employees. Each must calculate gratuity accurately and pay within the statutory timeline. Learn more about <a href="/gratuity-calculation-and-compliance-services">Gratuity Compliance across India</a>.</p>
                <p>Patron Accounting's Delhi office provides end-to-end gratuity compliance: calculation, employee register, Form F nominations, Ind AS 19 provisioning, LIC Group Gratuity advisory, new labour code wage restructuring, 30-day payment processing, and dispute resolution. With integrated <a href="/payroll-services">payroll services</a> and <a href="/pf-registration">PF registration</a>, Patron ensures seamless employer compliance.</p>
                <p>Content is reviewed quarterly for accuracy.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Gratuity: Statutory Retirement Benefit Under Indian Labour Law</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Gratuity is a statutory lump-sum payment by employer to employee as reward for long-term service under the Payment of Gratuity Act, 1972 (now Code on Social Security, 2020). It becomes payable on superannuation, resignation after 5 years, termination (unless for moral turpitude), or death/disablement (no minimum service).</p><p>The formula for covered employees: Gratuity = (Last Drawn Salary × 15 × Completed Years) / 26. Last drawn salary = basic + DA. 15 represents 15 days' wages per year. 26 = working days per month. For uncovered establishments (fewer than 10), the divisor is 30.</p><p>For Delhi employers - whether an IT company with 50 employees, a restaurant chain with 200 staff, a manufacturer with 100 workers, or a startup that crossed 10 employees - gratuity compliance is mandatory. Non-compliance attracts imprisonment up to 6 months and fines. Patron manages this as part of integrated payroll.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Gratuity Calculations & Compliance in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>15/26 Formula:</strong> (Last Drawn Salary × 15 × Completed Years) / 26 for Act-covered establishments. Divisor 30 for others.</p><p><strong>Last Drawn Salary:</strong> Basic Pay + Dearness Allowance at the time of leaving. Under new codes, wages must be ≥50% of CTC.</p><p><strong>Form F:</strong> Employee nomination form - mandatory within 30 days of completing 1 year of service.</p><p><strong>Controlling Authority:</strong> Delhi Labour Commissioner / Assistant Labour Commissioner for gratuity disputes.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
