                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How is gratuity calculated for Delhi employees?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Gratuity = (Last Drawn Salary × 15 × Completed Years) / 26. Last drawn salary = basic + DA. 15 represents 15 days' wages per year. 26 = working days per month. Service over 6 months in final year rounds up. Maximum Rs 20 lakh. Patron integrates with payroll.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Who is eligible for gratuity in Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Any employee completing 5 years continuous service in an establishment with 10+ employees. Under new codes, fixed-term employees qualify after 1 year pro-rata. Death/disablement: no minimum. All except apprentices are covered.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the maximum gratuity amount?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Rs 20 lakh for private sector. Rs 25 lakh for central government. Excess is taxable as income from salaries. The Rs 20 lakh is also the cumulative career limit for tax exemption.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What changed under the new labour codes?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Three key changes: (1) Fixed-term qualify after 1 year pro-rata. (2) Wages must be ≥50% of CTC, increasing gratuity base. (3) Broader coverage for gig workers. Patron advises on CTC restructuring.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What happens if employer delays payment?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>10% p.a. simple interest from due date. Employee can file complaint with Delhi Labour Commissioner. Employer faces up to Rs 10,000 fine or 6 months imprisonment.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can gratuity be forfeited?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Only for misconduct involving moral turpitude, violence, or riotous conduct during employment. Poor performance, absenteeism, or normal termination do not permit forfeiture.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is gratuity taxable?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Government employees: fully exempt. Private sector: exempt up to least of actual, Rs 20 lakh, or formula amount. Excess is taxable as income from salaries.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Do Delhi startups need to pay gratuity?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes, once 10+ employees at any point in preceding 12 months. Permanent once triggered. Many startups are unaware. Patron monitors headcount and alerts at threshold.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


